{
  "name": "CI Agent · B - Weekly Analyst Brief",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Workflow B — Weekly Analyst Agent + Human Approval\nEvery Monday the AI Agent (Gemini) reads the log, compares with last month and searches the web, then writes a partner-style brief: headline moves, SWOT delta, threats/opportunities and 3 actions. The brief is sent to Telegram for **Approve / Decline**. Approved briefs are marked **final**, emailed via Gmail and logged in the `Briefs` data table.",
        "width": 640,
        "height": 240,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "7c9a01f7-f6f2-4f28-ab30-7c185495a670",
      "name": "Note 1955b5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -200,
        -420
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "weeks",
              "triggerAtDay": [
                1
              ],
              "triggerAtHour": 9
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "9cf72179-4a3f-4f62-979e-0c7573c554f0",
      "name": "Every Monday 9 AM",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "7df5e436-5a2d-44cc-9bd6-1d540404bb26",
              "name": "telegram_chat_id",
              "value": "PASTE_YOUR_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "5bd120be-3548-4b97-9a53-6146fafa5229",
              "name": "brief_email",
              "value": "PASTE_RECIPIENT_EMAIL",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "cb125cfd-7dfb-4031-8fb9-408b293d8ac7",
      "name": "Config",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        220,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Today is {{ $now.toFormat('cccc, dd LLL yyyy') }}. Write this week's brief for the week starting {{ $now.minus({days: 7}).toFormat('dd LLL yyyy') }}.",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are a partner at a strategy consultancy writing the weekly competitive-intelligence brief for the Head of Product and the Head of Marketing of a company competing in the product-management / work-management software market (Notion, Atlassian Jira & Confluence, Asana, monday.com, Linear and similar tools).\n\nMethod:\n1. Call read_intel_log and focus on items whose `date` falls in the last 7 days (also use older items for context).\n2. Call compare_with_last_month with \"all\" to see month-over-month changes in activity.\n3. Use web_search only to verify or add context to the most important moves (max 3 searches).\n4. Ignore items with is_relevant = false or impact_score below 4 unless they form a pattern.\n\nWrite the brief in Markdown with exactly these sections:\n# Weekly Competitive Intelligence Brief — <week>\n## 1. Headline moves\n3-5 bullets: what changed, who, and why it matters (cite the impact score).\n## 2. SWOT delta per competitor\nFor each competitor with activity: one line each for new Strengths, Weaknesses, Opportunities, Threats revealed this week (write \"no change\" where nothing moved).\n## 3. Threats and opportunities for us\n## 4. Three recommended actions\nNumbered 1-3. Each: the action, owner (Product / Marketing / Leadership), priority (High/Medium), and why now.\n## 5. Sources\nBullet list of the links you relied on.\n\nRules: be concise and specific, no generic advice, never invent facts or links — if the week was quiet, say so. Mark recommendations as DRAFT; a human approves them before they become final.",
          "maxIterations": 12
        }
      },
      "id": "d5e1fae2-84f2-42c5-9a89-d5c721f95318",
      "name": "Analyst Agent",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        460,
        0
      ],
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 2,
      "waitBetweenTries": 5000
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "modelName": "models/gemini-2.5-flash",
        "options": {
          "temperature": 0.4
        }
      },
      "id": "785f2de8-11fa-4630-8bb1-22d29d3f8f23",
      "name": "Gemini 2.5 Flash",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatGoogleGemini",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        300,
        260
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "sessionIdType": "customKey",
        "sessionKey": "weekly-strategy-brief",
        "contextWindowLength": 6
      },
      "id": "71f17011-e15c-4e67-8653-1d03175fb6db",
      "name": "Window Buffer Memory",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.memoryBufferWindow",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "position": [
        440,
        260
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "descriptionType": "manual",
        "toolDescription": "Reads every logged competitor-intelligence item from the Intel_Log data table. Columns: date (logged), competitor, source_type, title, link, published, category (pricing/product_launch/hiring/partnership/campaign/other), impact_score (1-10), is_relevant, summary, reasoning, model_used, alerted.",
        "resource": "row",
        "operation": "get",
        "dataTableId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "Intel_Log",
          "mode": "name"
        },
        "returnAll": true
      },
      "id": "db3d5a4f-8eb9-48d3-b25a-48af15654c47",
      "name": "read_intel_log",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.dataTableTool",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        580,
        260
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "toolDescription": "Searches recent news (Google News RSS). Input: a short search query such as 'Asana pricing'. Returns RSS XML with titles, links and dates.",
        "url": "=https://news.google.com/rss/search?q={{ encodeURIComponent($fromAI('query', 'short news search query', 'string')) }}&hl=en-IN&gl=IN&ceid=IN:en",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "b80ba8b5-d455-4696-b1c6-8fcdbeb10e60",
      "name": "web_search",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequestTool",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        720,
        260
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "description": "Compares the last 30 days of logged competitor activity with the previous 30 days. Returns item counts, high-impact counts, average impact score and category mix per competitor. Input: a competitor name, or 'all'.",
        "workflowId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "__COMPARE_WORKFLOW_ID__",
          "mode": "id"
        },
        "workflowInputs": {
          "mappingMode": "defineBelow",
          "value": {
            "competitor": "={{ $fromAI('competitor', 'Competitor name exactly as logged, or all', 'string') }}"
          },
          "matchingColumns": [],
          "schema": [
            {
              "id": "competitor",
              "displayName": "competitor",
              "required": false,
              "defaultMatch": false,
              "display": true,
              "canBeUsedToMatch": true,
              "type": "string",
              "removed": false
            }
          ],
          "attemptToConvertTypes": false,
          "convertFieldsToString": false
        }
      },
      "id": "279d4d55-1dae-4489-8bbd-8a56568f0be4",
      "name": "compare_with_last_month",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.toolWorkflow",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        860,
        260
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "1e67f1cb-a4a9-4cf0-b142-8cd9133cac40",
              "name": "week",
              "value": "={{ $now.toFormat(\"kkkk-'W'WW\") }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "7a51d09e-b6d0-4588-9de3-ccf14384e8e8",
              "name": "brief_markdown",
              "value": "={{ $json.output }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "a04105bf-cbfe-469a-b8a4-1837f07597de",
              "name": "generated_at",
              "value": "={{ $now.toISO() }}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "152295f1-7fe2-49ff-88b1-d66132b65c95",
      "name": "Prepare Brief",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        820,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "sendAndWait",
        "chatId": "={{ $('Config').first().json.telegram_chat_id }}",
        "message": "=📋 Weekly brief {{ $json.week }} is ready for review (recommendations are DRAFT until you approve).\n\n{{ $json.brief_markdown.slice(0, 3300) }}{{ $json.brief_markdown.length > 3300 ? '\\n…(truncated)' : '' }}",
        "approvalOptions": {
          "values": {
            "approvalType": "double"
          }
        },
        "options": {
          "limitWaitTime": {
            "values": {
              "limitType": "afterTimeInterval",
              "resumeAmount": 48,
              "resumeUnit": "hours"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "id": "9b7708bc-7da6-4768-bbe7-4207eb98a597",
      "name": "Telegram Approval",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.telegram",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        1040,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "loose",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "1a9ad1cc-e1d2-4858-87df-78f258b85264",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.data.approved }}",
              "rightValue": "",
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "looseTypeValidation": true,
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "b5d45f33-4916-4058-86c8-df9050f798a8",
      "name": "Approved?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        1260,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "markdownToHtml",
        "markdown": "={{ $('Prepare Brief').item.json.brief_markdown.replace(/DRAFT/g, 'FINAL') }}",
        "destinationKey": "brief_html",
        "options": {
          "tables": true
        }
      },
      "id": "7c696e6c-d9a0-4b99-9382-fd1d6661f0d0",
      "name": "Markdown → HTML",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.markdown",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1480,
        -100
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "sendTo": "={{ $('Config').first().json.brief_email }}",
        "subject": "=Weekly Competitive Intelligence Brief — {{ $('Prepare Brief').item.json.week }}",
        "message": "={{ $json.brief_html }}",
        "options": {
          "appendAttribution": false
        }
      },
      "id": "0557a0b1-e5aa-427f-b208-cf3280c5e9c9",
      "name": "Email Brief (Gmail)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.gmail",
      "typeVersion": 2.1,
      "position": [
        1700,
        -100
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "raw",
        "jsonOutput": "={{ JSON.stringify({ week: $('Prepare Brief').item.json.week, generated_at: $('Prepare Brief').item.json.generated_at, status: 'final', brief: $('Prepare Brief').item.json.brief_markdown.replace(/DRAFT/g, 'FINAL') }) }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "8db421a2-c63e-4cef-ae08-11cd3d8f5281",
      "name": "Mark Final",
